      <h2>The 15-Minute Slicing Protocol: Avoid the Shatter Disaster</h2>
      <p>Commercial Dairy Queen holding freezers run between -10°F and -15°F to keep soft serve rigid during transport. Slicing the cake the moment you carry it inside will cause the hard outer shell to fracture into jagged clumps, pulverizing the crunch layer into dust. Follow this 4-step slicing ritual:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Countertop Acclimation:</strong> Open the cardboard tabs and let the cake rest undisturbed on your kitchen counter for exactly <strong>15 minutes</strong>. (If ambient room temperature exceeds 75°F, reduce this to 10 minutes).</li>
        <li><strong>Thermal Knife Bath:</strong> Fill a tall container with steaming hot water. Dip a long chef's knife into the bath for 20 seconds.</li>
        <li><strong>The Dry Wipe:</strong> Wipe the knife clean on a cloth towel before each cut. Water droplets create unappealing frost patches on the whipped icing.</li>
        <li><strong>The Single Downward Glide:</strong> Press firmly downward in one smooth pass. Never saw back and forth. Rinse and reheat the blade between each subsequent slice.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Custom Ordering Timeline: Grab-and-Go vs. Special Commissions</h2>
      <p>Depending on how specific your celebration needs are, consider these scheduling rules:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Same-Day Urgent Needs:</strong> Every franchise maintains a glass display case stocked with 8-inch and 10-inch round designs. The crew can pipe a custom name, age, or greeting in your choice of colored gel in under 5 minutes at zero extra charge.</li>
        <li><strong>Custom Blizzard &amp; Photo Cakes:</strong> Want a <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard-cake">Cookie Dough Blizzard Cake</a> topped with an edible photo icing portrait? You must contact your local store or use the online portal at least <strong>24 to 48 hours in advance</strong> so decorators have time to freeze the custom blend solid before decorating.</li>
      </ul>

